를 사용한 파일 기반의 라우팅 설정","React Native와 TypeScript의 지원","Stack과 Tabs 컴포넌트의 통합","Safe Area를 사용한 안전 영역 설정","테마와 스타일의 설정 지원","Core 컴포넌트를 사용한 인터페이스 개발"],"es":["Uso de Expo Router para la configuración de rutas","Creación de pantallas con React Native y TypeScript","Soporte para Stack y Tabs de expo-router","Uso de Safe Area via react-native-safe-area-context","Compatibilidad con temas personalizados a través de useAppTheme y useStyles"],"fr":["Utilisation d''Expo Router pour la configuration des routes","Création d''écrans avec React Native et TypeScript","Prise en charge de Stack et Tabs d''expo-router","Utilisation de Safe Area via react-native-safe-area-context","Compatibilité avec les thèmes personnalisés via useAppTheme et useStyles"],"de":["Verwendung von Expo Router für die Routenkonfiguration","Erstellung von Bildschirmen mit React Native und TypeScript","Unterstützung für Stack und Tabs von expo-router","Verwendung von Safe Area via react-native-safe-area-context","Kompatibilität mit benutzerdefinierten Themen über useAppTheme und useStyles"],"pt":["Uso de Expo Router para roteamento baseado em arquivos","Criação de telas com React Native e TypeScript","Uso de Stack e Tabs para navegação","Integração com Safe Area para melhor experiência do usuário","Uso de componentes core e ícones para interface do usuário"],"ru":["Использование Expo Router для маршрутизации на основе файлов","Создание экранов с помощью React Native и TypeScript","Использование Stack и Tabs для навигации","Интеграция с Safe Area для лучшего пользовательского опыта","Использование базовых компонентов и иконок для интерфейса пользователя с помощью ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["استخدام Expo Router لتصفية الطرق بالاعتماد على الملفات","إنشاء الشاشات باستخدام React Native و TypeScript","استخدام Stack و Tabs للملاحة","التكامل مع Safe Area لتحسين تجربة المستخدم","استخدام المكونات الأساسية والأيقونات لواجهة المستخدم مع أدوات الإصطناع الإعتيادي"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use create-screens-and-routing","create-screens-and-routing setup guide","Expo Router tutorial","React Native routing configuration","create-screens-and-routing alternative","create-screens-and-routing vs React Navigation","install create-screens-and-routing","create-screens-and-routing documentation","what is create-screens-and-routing"],"zh":["AI工具","创建屏幕","路由配置","Expo Router","React Native","文件基于路由","Stack","Tabs","Safe Area"],"ja":["AIエージェント","スクリーンの作成","ルーティングの設定","Expo Router","React Native","ファイルベースのルーティング","Stack","Tabs","Safe Area"],"ko":["AI 도구","화면 생성","라우팅 설정","Expo Router","React Native","파일 기반의 라우팅","Stack","Tabs","Safe Area"],"es":["create-screens-and-routing","Expo Router","React Native","TypeScript","Stack y Tabs","Safe Area","Temas personalizados","Desarrollo de aplicaciones móviles","Herramientas de IA para desarrollo"],"fr":["create-screens-and-routing","Expo Router","React Native","TypeScript","Stack et Tabs","Safe Area","Thèmes personnalisés","Développement d''applications mobiles","Outils d''IA pour le développement"],"de":["create-screens-and-routing","Expo Router","React Native","TypeScript","Stack und Tabs","Safe Area","Benutzerdefinierte Themen","Entwicklung von mobilen Anwendungen","AI-Tools für die Entwicklung"],"pt":["criar telas e roteamento","Expo Router","React Native","TypeScript","roteamento baseado em arquivos","navegação em aplicativos móveis","componentes core","ícones para interface do usuário"],"ru":["создание экранов и маршрутизации","Expo Router","React Native","TypeScript","маршрутизация на основе файлов","навигация в мобильных приложениях","ИИ Агенты","базовые компоненты","иконки для интерфейса пользователя"],"ar":["إنشاء الشاشات وتصفية الطرق","Expo Router","React Native","TypeScript","تصفية الطرق بالاعتماد على الملفات","الملاحة في التطبيقات المحمولة","أدوات الإصطناع الإعتيادي","المكونات الأساسية","الأيقونات لواجهة المستخدم"]}},"owner":"Vinicius-B-Leite","repo":"blcalisteniaV2","repoPath":"Vinicius-B-Leite/blcalisteniaV2","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.476Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"create-screens-and-routing","description":"Creates screens and configures routing with Expo Router following project patterns: file-based routes, route groups, protected routes, screen components with hooks and theme styles. Use when adding new screens, tabs, layouts, or when the user asks about navigation and routing.","bodyPreview":"# Creating Screens and Routing\n\nThis skill guides the creation of screens and routing configuration using Expo Router and the project''s screen/layout patterns.\n\n## Technologies & Stack\n\n- **Expo Router** (file-based routing)\n- **React Native** with TypeScript\n- **Stack** and **Tabs** from `expo-router`\n- **Safe Area** via `react-native-safe-area-context`\n- **Theme** via `useAppTheme` and `useStyles`\n- **Core components** from `src/ui/components/core/` (Screen, Text, Button, Icon, etc.)\n- **Icons","body":"# Creating Screens and Routing\n\nThis skill guides the creation of screens and routing configuration using Expo Router and the project''s screen/layout patterns.\n\n## Technologies & Stack\n\n- **Expo Router** (file-based routing)\n- **React Native** with TypeScript\n- **Stack** and **Tabs** from `expo-router`\n- **Safe Area** via `react-native-safe-area-context`\n- **Theme** via `useAppTheme` and `useStyles`\n- **Core components** from `src/ui/components/core/` (Screen, Text, Button, Icon, etc.)\n- **Icons**: use only the core `Icon` component. Do not use `@expo/vector-icons`, `Ionicons`, or any other icon library directly.\n\n## Concepts\n\n### Route file vs Screen component\n\n- **Route file** (`src/app/...`): Thin entry point that only imports and renders the screen component. No layout/UI logic here.\n- **Screen component** (`src/ui/screens/...`): Actual UI, hooks, and styles. Reusable and testable.\n\n### Route groups\n\nParentheses create **groups** (no segment in URL): `(application)`, `(tabs)`.\n\n- Use for layout nesting without changing the URL.\n- Example: `(application)/(tabs)/home` → URL `/home`, not `/(application)/(tabs)/home`.\n\n## App structure (src/app)\n\n```\napp/\n├── _layout.tsx           # Root layout: ThemeProvider, SafeAreaProvider, AuthProvider, Stack\n├── index.tsx             # Entry route (e.g. onboarding) → renders OnboardingScreen\n└── (application)/        # Route group (protected)\n    ├── _layout.tsx       # Protected layout: redirect if not auth, Stack with (tabs)\n    └── (tabs)/           # Route group for tab navigation\n        ├── _layout.tsx   # Tabs layout\n        └── home.tsx      # Tab screen\n```\n\n## Route file pattern\n\nRoute files are minimal: default export that renders the screen component.\n\n```tsx\n// src/app/(application)/(tabs)/home.tsx\nimport { HomeScreen } from \"../../../ui/screens/Home/Home\"\n\nexport default function Home() {\n\treturn <HomeScreen />\n}\n```\n\n**Rules:**\n\n- One default export (the page component).\n- No business logic or layout in the route file; delegate to the screen.\n\n## Screen component structure (src/ui/screens)\n\nEach feature screen lives in its own folder:\n\n```\nScreenName/\n├── ScreenName.tsx      # Main screen component\n├── styles.ts           # Theme-based styles (stylesTheme)\n├── useScreenName.ts    # Hook: actions, states, refs (UI only)\n├── components/         # Optional: screen-specific components\n│   └── Header/\n│       ├── Header.tsx\n│       ├── styles.ts\n│       └── index.ts\n└── __tests__/          # Optional\n    └── ScreenName.test.tsx\n```\n\nA screen folder may include a **`components/`** subfolder for components used only by that screen. If a component is reused across screens, place it in `src/ui/components/core/` or a shared components folder instead.\n\n### Screen-specific components (components/)\n\nComponents in `components/` follow this structure:\n\n```\nScreenName/components/ComponentName/\n├── ComponentName.tsx\n├── styles.ts                 # Optional: stylesTheme(theme) when component has its own styles\n└── index.ts                  # export { ComponentName } from \"./ComponentName\"\n```\n\n**Patterns:**\n\n- Props receive data and callbacks from the parent screen (e.g. `userName`, `onNotificationsPress`). The screen hook provides `states` and `actions`; pass them down as props.\n- Use core components: `Text`, `Button`, **`Icon`** (never `Ionicons` or other icon libs directly).\n- Use `useAppTheme()` and `stylesTheme(theme)` in component styles when the component has its own styles.\n- Use theme tokens (`theme.action[\"brand-primary\"]`, `spacings`, `radius`) in styles.\n- Component styles file: `styles.ts` in the component folder, exporting `stylesTheme(theme: ThemeType)`.\n\n**Example: Header component (Home screen)**\n\n```\nHome/components/Header/\n├── Header.tsx\n├── styles.ts\n└── index.ts\n```\n\n```tsx\n// Header.tsx\nimport { Image, View } from \"react-native\"\nimport { Text } from \"../../../../components/core/Text/Text\"\nimport { Icon } from \"../../../../components/core/Icon\"\nimport { useAppTheme } from \"../../../../theme/hooks/useAppTheme\"\nimport { stylesTheme } from \"./styles\"\n\ntype HeaderProps = {\n\tuserName: string\n\tonNotificationsPress: () => void\n}\n\nexport function Header({ userName, onNotificationsPress }: HeaderProps) {\n\tconst { theme } = useAppTheme()\n\tconst styles = stylesTheme(theme)\n\n\treturn (\n\t\t<View style={styles.row}>\n\t\t\t<View style={styles.leftContent}>\n\t\t\t\t<View style={styles.avatarContainer}>\n\t\t\t\t\t<Image source={{ uri: \"...\" }} style={styles.avatar} />\n\t\t\t\t</View>\n\t\t\t\t<View style={styles.textContainer}>\n\t\t\t\t\t<Text variant=\"title-large-bold\">Olá, {userName}!</Text>\n\t\t\t\t\t<Text variant=\"title-small-reg\">Vamos treinar hoje?</Text>\n\t\t\t\t</View>\n\t\t\t</View>\n\t\t\t<Icon\n\t\t\t\tonPress={onNotificationsPress}\n\t\t\t\tpressableStyle={styles.bellButton}\n\t\t\t\tname=\"icon-notification\"\n\t\t\t\tsize={21}\n\t\t\t\tvariant=\"default\"\n\t\t\t/>\n\t\t</View>\n\t)\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// styles.ts\nimport { StyleSheet } from \"react-native\"\nimport { ThemeType } from \"../../../../theme\"\nimport { radius } from \"../../../../theme/tokens/sizes\"\nimport { spacings } from \"../../../../theme/tokens/spacings\"\n\nconst AVATAR_SIZE = 48\n\nexport const stylesTheme = (theme: ThemeType) =>\n\tStyleSheet.create({\n\t\trow: {\n\t\t\tflexDirection: \"row\",\n\t\t\talignItems: \"center\",\n\t\t\tjustifyContent: \"space-between\",\n\t\t\tgap: spacings.padding[8],\n\t\t},\n\t\tavatarContainer: {\n\t\t\twidth: AVATAR_SIZE,\n\t\t\theight: AVATAR_SIZE,\n\t\t\tborderRadius: AVATAR_SIZE / 2,\n\t\t\toverflow: \"hidden\",\n\t\t\tbackgroundColor: theme.action[\"brand-primary\"],\n\t\t},\n\t\tavatar: {\n\t\t\twidth: AVATAR_SIZE,\n\t\t\theight: AVATAR_SIZE,\n\t\t},\n\t})\n```\n\n**Usage in screen:**\n\n```tsx\n// Home.tsx\n<Header\n\tuserName={states.userName}\n\tonNotificationsPress={actions.handleNotificationsPress}\n/>\n```\n\n### Screen component\n\n- **Always use the core `Screen` component as the main container** of the screen. No other root wrapper (e.g. plain `View`) for the whole screen.\n- Receives no route params in the component signature unless the route passes them.\n- Uses a custom hook that returns `actions`, `states`, and `refs`.\n- Uses `useStyles` with a `stylesTheme(theme, ...)` function for styles.\n- Prefer core components: `Screen`, `Text`, `Button`, `Icon`, etc. **Icons must use the core `Icon` component only**—no `Ionicons`, `@expo/vector-icons`, or other icon libs.\n\n```tsx\n// ScreenName.tsx\nimport { View } from \"react-native\"\nimport { Text } from \"../../components/core/Text/Text\"\nimport { Screen } from \"../../components/core/Screen/Screen\"\nimport { useStyles } from \"../../theme/hooks/useStyles\"\nimport { stylesTheme } from \"./styles\"\nimport { useScreenName } from \"./useScreenName\"\n\nexport function ScreenNameScreen() {\n\tconst { actions, states, refs } = useScreenName()\n\tconst styles = useStyles((theme) => stylesTheme(theme, states.insets))\n\n\treturn (\n\t\t<Screen>\n\t\t\t<View style={styles.container} ref={refs.containerRef}>\n\t\t\t\t<Text variant=\"heading\">Title</Text>\n\t\t\t\t{/* ... */}\n\t\t\t</View>\n\t\t</Screen>\n\t)\n}\n```\n\n### styles.ts\n\n- Export a function `stylesTheme(theme: ThemeType, ...deps)` that returns a `StyleSheet.create(...)`.\n- Use theme tokens: `theme.surface.background`, `spacings`, etc.\n- Use safe area insets when needed (e.g. bottom padding).\n\n```typescript\n// styles.ts\nimport { StyleSheet } from \"react-native\"\nimport { ThemeType } from \"../../theme\"\nimport { spacings } from \"../../theme/tokens/spacings\"\nimport { EdgeInsets } from \"react-native-safe-area-context\"\n\nexport const stylesTheme = (theme: ThemeType, insets: EdgeInsets) =>\n\tStyleSheet.create({\n\t\tcontainer: {\n\t\t\tflex: 1,\n\t\t\tgap: spacings.gap[32],\n\t\t\tpaddingBottom:\n\t\t\t\tMath.max(insets.bottom, spacings.padding[20]) + spacings.padding[20],\n\t\t},\n\t})\n```\n\n### useScreenName hook\n\n- **Return always** `{ actions, states, refs }`. Even if one category is empty, expose the key (e.g. `refs: {}`).\n- **UI rules only**: no business logic. The hook handles only UI concerns: navigation (e.g. `useRouter`), safe area, theme, refs, local UI state (e.g. focus, visibility). Business rules (validation, API calls, domain logic) belong in domain/use cases, not in the screen hook.\n- `actions`: handlers for user interactions (e.g. navigate, toggle, submit that delegates to a service).\n- `states`: derived or reactive values for rendering (e.g. `insets`, `theme`, loading flags coming from props/context).\n- `refs`: refs for DOM/native elements used by the screen (e.g. scroll ref, input ref). Use `useRef` and expose them in `refs`.\n\n```typescript\n// useScreenName.ts\nimport { useRef } from \"react\"\nimport { View } from \"react-native\"\nimport { useSafeAreaInsets } from \"react-native-safe-area-context\"\nimport { useRouter } from \"expo-router\"\nimport { useAppTheme } from \"../../theme/hooks/useAppTheme\"\n\nexport const useScreenName = () => {\n\tconst router = useRouter()\n\tconst insets = useSafeAreaInsets()\n\tconst { theme } = useAppTheme()\n\tconst containerRef = useRef<View>(null)\n\n\tconst handleNavigate = () => {\n\t\trouter.navigate(\"/other-route\")\n\t}\n\n\treturn {\n\t\tactions: { handleNavigate },\n\t\tstates: { insets, theme },\n\t\trefs: { containerRef },\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n## Root layout (\\_layout.tsx)\n\n- Wraps app with: `ThemeProvider` → `SafeAreaProvider` → `AuthProvider` → routing.\n- Uses `Stack` from `expo-router`.\n- Uses `Stack.Protected` with `guard={!!auth?.id}` for protected routes.\n- Entry route: `name=\"index\"` with `headerShown: false`.\n\n```tsx\nconst Routes = () => {\n\tconst { auth } = useAuth()\n\treturn (\n\t\t<Stack>\n\t\t\t<Stack.Screen name=\"index\" options={{ headerShown: false }} />\n\t\t\t<Stack.Protected guard={!!auth?.id}>\n\t\t\t\t<Stack.Screen name=\"(application)\" />\n\t\t\t</Stack.Protected>\n\t\t</Stack>\n\t)\n}\n```\n\n## Protected layout (e.g. (application)/\\_layout.tsx)\n\n- Redirect to entry if not authenticated.\n- Use `Stack` with `screenOptions`: `headerShown: false`, `fullScreenGestureEnabled: true` as in the project.\n\n```tsx\nimport { Redirect, Stack } from \"expo-router\"\nimport { useAuth } from \"../../domain/auth/AuthContext\"\n\nexport default function ProtectedLayout() {\n\tconst { auth } = useAuth()\n\tif (!auth?.id) return <Redirect href=\"/\" />\n\treturn (\n\t\t<Stack screenOptions={{ headerShown: false, fullScreenGestureEnabled: true }}>\n\t\t\t<Stack.Screen name=\"(tabs)\" />\n\t\t</Stack>\n\t)\n}\n```\n\n## Tabs layout\n\n- Use `Tabs` from `expo-router`.\n- One `Tabs.Screen` per tab file (e.g. `home`, `profile`).\n\n```tsx\nimport { Tabs } from \"expo-router\"\n\nexport default function TabLayout() {\n\treturn (\n\t\t<Tabs>\n\t\t\t<Tabs.Screen name=\"home\" />\n\t\t\t<Tabs.Screen name=\"profile\" />\n\t\t</Tabs>\n\t)\n}\n```\n\n## Adding a new screen (step-by-step)\n\n### 1. Screen folder and files\n\n- Create `src/ui/screens/FeatureName/FeatureName.tsx` (export `FeatureNameScreen`).\n- Create `src/ui/screens/FeatureName/styles.ts` with `stylesTheme(theme, ...)`.\n- Create `src/ui/screens/FeatureName/useFeatureName.ts` with `useFeatureName()` returning `{ actions, states, refs }` (UI-only, no business logic).\n\n### 2. Route file\n\n- Create the route file in `src/app/` according to desired URL:\n    - Tab: `(application)/(tabs)/featureName.tsx`\n    - Stack inside app: `(application)/featureName.tsx`\n    - Entry-level: e.g. `someRoute.tsx` and register in root `_layout.tsx` if needed.\n- In the route file: import the screen and default-export a function that renders it.\n\n### 3. Register in layout (if needed)\n\n- New tab: add `<Tabs.Screen name=\"featureName\" />` in `(application)/(tabs)/_layout.tsx`.\n- New stack screen: add `<Stack.Screen name=\"featureName\" />` in the corresponding `_layout.tsx`.\n\n## Navigation\n\n- Use `useRouter()` from `expo-router`: `router.push(href)`, `router.replace(href)`, `router.back()`.\n- Use path strings: `\"/\"`, `\"/home\"`, `\"/(application)/(tabs)/profile\"` (group names don’t appear in URL).\n- Use `<Link href=\"...\">` for declarative navigation when appropriate.\n\n## Naming conventions\n\n- **Route files**: camelCase, e.g. `home.tsx`, `featureName.tsx`.\n- **Screen folder**: PascalCase, e.g. `Onboarding`, `Home`, `FeatureName`.\n- **Screen component**: `ScreenNameScreen` (e.g. `OnboardingScreen`, `HomeScreen`).\n- **Hook**: `useScreenName` (e.g. `useOnboarding`, `useHome`).\n- **Styles**: `stylesTheme` in `styles.ts`.\n\n## Checklist\n\nWhen creating a new screen and route:\n\n- [ ] Created folder `src/ui/screens/FeatureName/` with `FeatureName.tsx`, `styles.ts`, `useFeatureName.ts`.\n- [ ] Screen uses **core `Screen`** as the main container (root wrapper of the screen).\n- [ ] Screen hook returns `{ actions, states, refs }`; hook contains **only UI rules**, no business logic.\n- [ ] Styles use `stylesTheme(theme, ...)` and `useStyles`.\n- [ ] Used core components and theme tokens. **Icons only via core `Icon`** (no Ionicons/vector-icons directly).\n- [ ] Created route file in `src/app/` that only renders the screen component.\n- [ ] Registered the route in the correct `_layout.tsx` (Stack or Tabs).\n- [ ] Navigation uses `useRouter()` or `<Link>` with correct paths.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:09:47.865Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Mobile App Agents needing streamlined screen creation and routing configuration with Expo Router and React Native.","zh":"非常适合需要使用 Expo Router 和 React Native 进行流畅的屏幕创建和路由配置的移动应用代理。","ja":"Expo RouterとReact Nativeを使用してスムーズなスクリーン作成とルーティング構成が必要なモバイルアプリエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Expo Router와 React Native를 사용하여 원활한 화면 생성 및 라우팅 구성이 필요한 모바일 앱 에이전트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Aplicaciones Móviles que necesitan una creación de pantalla y configuración de enrutamiento simplificadas con Expo Router y React Native.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''applications mobiles ayant besoin d''une création d''écran et d''une configuration de routage simplifiées avec Expo Router et React Native.","de":"Perfekt für Mobile App-Agents, die eine vereinfachte Bildschirm- und Routing-Konfiguration mit Expo Router und React Native benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Aplicativos Móveis que precisam de criação de tela e configuração de roteamento simplificadas com Expo Router e React Native.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Мобильных Агентских Приложений, которым необходима упрощенная создание экранов и настройка маршрутизации с помощью Expo Router и React Native.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطبيق المحمول الذي يحتاج إلى إنشاء شاشة وتكوين маршーティング مبسطين مع Expo Router و React Native."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate robust mobile application screens using Expo Router''s file-based routing, React Native with TypeScript, and integrate seamlessly with Stack, Tabs, and Safe Area components, all while leveraging a customizable theme via useAppTheme and useStyles.","zh":"赋予代理生成强大的移动应用程序屏幕的能力，使用Expo Router的文件 기반路由、React Native与TypeScript，并与Stack、Tabs和Safe Area组件无缝集成，同时利用useAppTheme和useStyles实现可定制的主题。","ja":"Expo Routerのファイルベースのルーティング、React Native with TypeScript、およびStack、Tabs、Safe Areaコンポーネントとシームレスに統合して、強力なモバイルアプリケーションスクリーンを生成するエージェントを可能にし、useAppThemeとuseStylesを使用してカスタマイズ可能なテーマを利用します。","ko":"Expo Router의 파일 기반 라우팅, React Native with TypeScript 및 Stack, Tabs, Safe Area 컴포넌트와의 무결점 통합을 통해 강력한 모바일 애플리케이션 스크린을 생성할 수 있는 에이전트를 활성화하고 useAppTheme 및 useStyles를 사용하여 사용자 정의 가능한 테마를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar pantallas de aplicaciones móviles robustas utilizando el enrutamiento basado en archivos de Expo Router, React Native con TypeScript, e integrarse de forma transparente con los componentes Stack, Tabs y Safe Area, todo mientras aprovecha un tema personalizable a través de useAppTheme y useStyles.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des écrans d''applications mobiles robustes en utilisant le routage basé sur des fichiers d''Expo Router, React Native avec TypeScript, et de s''intégrer de manière transparente avec les composants Stack, Tabs et Safe Area, le tout en exploitant un thème personnalisable via useAppTheme et useStyles.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, robuste mobile Anwendungsbildschirme zu generieren, die Expo Routers dateibasiertes Routing, React Native mit TypeScript und eine nahtlose Integration mit Stack-, Tabs- und Safe-Area-Komponenten verwenden, alles bei der Nutzung eines anpassbaren Themas über useAppTheme und useStyles.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar telas de aplicativos móveis robustas usando o roteamento baseado em arquivos do Expo Router, React Native com TypeScript e integrar-se perfeitamente com os componentes Stack, Tabs e Safe Area, tudo isso aproveitando um tema personalizável via useAppTheme e useStyles.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать прочные мобильные приложения с использованием файлового маршрутизации Expo Router, React Native с TypeScript и бесшовной интеграции с компонентами Stack, Tabs и Safe Area, все это при помощи настраиваемой темы через useAppTheme и useStyles.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من توليد شاشات تطبيقات محمول قوية باستخدام التوجيه المبني على الملفات في Expo Router و React Native مع TypeScript وتكاملها بشكل متجانس مع مكونات Stack و Tabs و Safe Area ، كل ذلك مع الاستفادة من موضوع قابل للتخصيص عبر useAppTheme و useStyles."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating responsive screens with Expo Router''s file-based routing","Configuring navigation flows using Stack and Tabs from expo-router","Implementing safe area layouts with react-native-safe-area-context"],"zh":["使用Expo Router的文件基于路由创建响应式屏幕","使用Stack和Tabs从expo-router配置导航流程","使用react-native-safe-area-context实现安全区域布局"],"ja":["Expo Routerのファイルベースのルーティングを使用してレスポンシブスクリーンを作成する","StackとTabsからexpo-routerを使用してナビゲーションフローを構成する","react-native-safe-area-contextを使用してセーフエリアレイアウトを実装する"],"ko":["Expo Router의 파일 기반 라우팅을 사용하여 반응형 화면을 생성하는 것","Stack 및 Tabs에서 expo-router를 사용하여 네비게이션 흐름을 구성하는 것","react-native-safe-area-context를 사용하여 안전 영역 레이아웃을 구현하는 것"],"es":["Crear pantallas responsivas con el enrutamiento basado en archivos de Expo Router","Configurar flujos de navegación utilizando Stack y Tabs de expo-router","Implementar diseños de área segura con react-native-safe-area-context"],"fr":["Créer des écrans réactifs avec le routage basé sur des fichiers d''Expo Router","Configurer des flux de navigation en utilisant Stack et Tabs d''expo-router","Mettre en œuvre des dispositions de zone sûre avec react-native-safe-area-context"],"de":["Erstellen von responsiven Bildschirmen mit dem dateibasierten Routing von Expo Router","Konfigurieren von Navigationsflüssen unter Verwendung von Stack und Tabs von expo-router","Implementieren von sicheren Bereichslayouts mit react-native-safe-area-context"],"pt":["Criando telas responsivas com o roteamento baseado em arquivos do Expo Router","Configurando fluxos de navegação usando Stack e Tabs do expo-router","Implementando layouts de área segura com react-native-safe-area-context"],"ru":["Создание адаптивных экранов с помощью файлового маршрутизации Expo Router","Настройка потоков навигации с помощью Stack и Tabs из expo-router","Реализация безопасных макетов с помощью react-native-safe-area-context"],"ar":["إنشاء شاشات مستجيبة باستخدام التوجيه المبني على الملفات في Expo Router","تكوين تدفقات الملاحة باستخدام Stack و Tabs من expo-router","تنفيذ تخطيطات منطقة آمنة مع react-native-safe-area-context"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Expo Router and React Native setup","Limited to mobile application development","Dependent on TypeScript for type checking and compilation"],"zh":["需要Expo Router和React Native设置","仅限移动应用程序开发","依赖TypeScript进行类型检查和编译"],"ja":["Expo RouterとReact Nativeの設定が必要","モバイルアプリケーションの開発に限定される","TypeScriptに依存して型チェックとコンパイルを行う"],"ko":["Expo Router 및 React Native 설정이 필요함","모바일 애플리케이션 개발에만 제한됨","타입스크립트에 의존하여 타입 체크 및 컴파일을 수행함"],"es":["Requiere la configuración de Expo Router y React Native","Limitado al desarrollo de aplicaciones móviles","Dependiente de TypeScript para la comprobación y compilación de tipos"],"fr":["Nécessite la configuration d''Expo Router et de React Native","Limité au développement d''applications mobiles","Dépendant de TypeScript pour la vérification et la compilation des types"],"de":["Benötigt die Einrichtung von Expo Router und React Native","Begrenzt auf die Entwicklung von mobilen Anwendungen","Abhängig von TypeScript für die Typüberprüfung und -kompilierung"],"pt":["Requer configuração do Expo Router e React Native","Limitado ao desenvolvimento de aplicativos móveis","Dependente do TypeScript para verificação e compilação de tipos"],"ru":["Требует настройки Expo Router и React Native","Ограничен разработкой мобильных приложений","Зависит от TypeScript для проверки и компиляции типов"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد Expo Router و React Native","محدود بتطوير التطبيقات المحمول","يت phụ thuộc على TypeScript لتحقق و تجميع الأنواع"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"32dedd07a76ddb724a48a9b9a829f6711648ef5d8efeabf7973d09f5a7f48d25","qualityScore":39}');
